    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0382" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg376"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/24340: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers (Cole) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-18T13:00:00+01:00">September 18,
                            1942—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 18—11:01 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>613. For Murphy. Our saintly friend<anchor n="56" xml:id="d368-f1"/> here reports
                    that the other friends, the flagpole sitter,<anchor n="56" xml:id="d368-f2"/>
                    are anxious to know what has become of the projected secret meeting of their and
                    our “general staffs” which they state was tentatively planned for September 15
                    somewhere in North Africa.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cole</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
